  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b1_u02_l2_g1",
      "pattern": "Salomlashish va xayrlashish",
      "meaning_uz": "안녕하세요, 안녕히 가세요, 안녕히 계세요",
      "meaning_en": "Hello and goodbye",
      "explanation_md": "Koreyschada salomlashish bitta, xayrlashish esa **ikkita** — kim ketayotganiga qarab.\n\n- **안녕하세요?** — *Assalomu alaykum / Salom* (kunning istalgan vaqtida)\n- **안녕히 가세요.** — *Xayr* — **ketayotgan** odamga (so'zma-so'z: \"tinch boring\")\n- **안녕히 계세요.** — *Xayr* — **qolayotgan** odamga (\"tinch qoling\")\n\n### Kim nima deydi\n\nSiz o'qituvchidan **ketyapsiz** → **선생님, 안녕히 계세요.**  \nO'qituvchi **qoladi** va sizga → **안녕히 가세요.**  \nIkkalangiz ham ketsangiz → **안녕히 가세요.**\n\n### Boshqa kerakli iboralar\n\n- **감사합니다 / 고맙습니다** — *Rahmat*\n- **죄송합니다 / 미안합니다** — *Kechirasiz*\n- **괜찮아요** — *Hechqisi yo'q*\n- **또 만나요** — *Yana ko'rishamiz*",
      "explanation_md_en": "Korean has one hello but **two goodbyes**, depending on who is leaving.\n\n- **안녕하세요?** — *Hello* (any time of day)\n- **안녕히 가세요.** — *Goodbye* — to someone **leaving** (literally \"go in peace\")\n- **안녕히 계세요.** — *Goodbye* — to someone **staying** (\"stay in peace\")\n\n### Who says what\n\nYou're **leaving** the teacher → **선생님, 안녕히 계세요.**  \nThe teacher **stays** and says to you → **안녕히 가세요.**  \nIf you both leave → **안녕히 가세요.**\n\n### Other useful phrases\n\n- **감사합니다 / 고맙습니다** — *Thank you*\n- **죄송합니다 / 미안합니다** — *Sorry*\n- **괜찮아요** — *It's okay*\n- **또 만나요** — *See you again*",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Uchrashganda",
          "condition_en": "Meeting",
          "rule": "안녕하세요?",
          "example": "선생님, 안녕하세요?"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ketayotganga",
          "condition_en": "To someone leaving",
          "rule": "안녕히 가세요",
          "example": "민지 씨, 안녕히 가세요."
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Qolayotganga",
          "condition_en": "To someone staying",
          "rule": "안녕히 계세요",
          "example": "선생님, 안녕히 계세요."
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
