      "meaning_uz": "Rasmiy uslub: ...man, ...miz",
      "meaning_en": "Formal style",
      "explanation_md": "**-(스)ㅂ니다** — **rasmiy** uslub. Sinfda, yangiliklarda, taqdimotda, notanish katta odamlar bilan ishlatiladi. Ko'p tayyor iboralar shu shaklda: **감사합니다**, **알겠습니다**, **죄송합니다**.\n\n**질문 있습니다.** — *Savolim bor.*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n- O'zak **받침siz** → **-ㅂ니다**: 가다 → **갑니다**, 감사하다 → **감사합니다**\n- O'zak **받침 bilan** → **-습니다**: 먹다 → **먹습니다**, 있다 → **있습니다**\n- O'zak **ㄹ bilan** → ㄹ tushadi + **-ㅂ니다**: 알다 → **압니다**, 만들다 → **만듭니다**\n\n### So'roq shakli\n\n**-ㅂ니까? / -습니까?**: **질문 있습니까?** — *Savol bormi?*\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Kundalik suhbatda **-아요/어요** (6-1) ko'proq ishlatiladi. **-ㅂ니다** — rasmiyroq.\n- **N입니다** = **N이에요/예요** ning rasmiy shakli: **저는 아지즈입니다.**",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-(스)ㅂ니다** is the **formal** style, used in class, in the news, in presentations and with older strangers. Many set phrases use it: **감사합니다**, **알겠습니다**, **죄송합니다**.\n\n**질문 있습니다.** — *I have a question.*\n\n### How to form it\n\n- Stem **without 받침** → **-ㅂ니다**: 가다 → **갑니다**, 감사하다 → **감사합니다**\n- Stem **with 받침** → **-습니다**: 먹다 → **먹습니다**, 있다 → **있습니다**\n- Stem **ending in ㄹ** → drop ㄹ + **-ㅂ니다**: 알다 → **압니다**, 만들다 → **만듭니다**\n\n### Questions\n\n**-ㅂ니까? / -습니까?**: **질문 있습니까?** — *Any questions?*\n\n### Remember\n\n- Everyday conversation mostly uses **-아요/어요** (6-1). **-ㅂ니다** sounds more formal.\n- **N입니다** is the formal form of **N이에요/예요**: **저는 아지즈입니다.**",
      "formation": [
